From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d012 setup <setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] The mods folder button asks the profile where the mods are

Open the mods folder opened the mods folder of the data folder, which is not where a mod that the player placed (an Android download into the app storage or an SD card) keeps its files. A profile can now say where they are (GameProfile::mods_folder); without it the button opens the data folder as before.
---

diff --git a/host/profile.hpp b/host/profile.hpp
index 5b834ea..b8b448e 100644
--- a/host/profile.hpp
+++ b/host/profile.hpp
@@ -240,6 +240,10 @@ struct GameProfile {
     // leaves hosts of the other edition out. Both unset: no editions.
     char adhoc_edition_mark = 0;
     bool (*adhoc_edition_active)() = nullptr;
+    // Where the mod data actually is, as a UTF-8 path, for the Mods page's "Open the mods folder" button. A game that lets the player
+    // choose where it goes (an Android download into the app's storage or an SD card) answers with that folder; empty, or unset: the
+    // mods folder of the data folder.
+    std::string (*mods_folder)() = nullptr;
     // A public ad hoc server (this port's own stand-alone relay) that players connect out to, so nobody forwards a port: "host" or
     // "host:port". Empty: none. A room name (the Room setting) is folded into the product code, so players in different rooms never
     // meet on it. The Network page offers it first and falls back to hosting with an opened router port when it cannot be reached.
diff --git a/host/ui/menu.cpp b/host/ui/menu.cpp
index 759f233..a53429f 100644
--- a/host/ui/menu.cpp
+++ b/host/ui/menu.cpp
@@ -1831,8 +1831,11 @@ void Menu::cheats() {
 
 void Menu::mods() {
     section("Mods");
-    if (button_row("Open the mods folder", {false, {}, "Show the mods folder in the data folder."}))
-        open_folder(install::user_data_directory() / "mods");
+    if (button_row("Open the mods folder", {false, {}, "Show the folder the mods are in."})) {
+        const portablekit::GameProfile &profile = portablekit::game();
+        const std::string chosen = profile.mods_folder != nullptr ? profile.mods_folder() : std::string();
+        open_folder(chosen.empty() ? install::user_data_directory() / "mods" : install::path_from_utf8(chosen));
+    }
     for (void (*rows)() : mod_rows()) rows();
 }
 
